    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010394": {
      "title": "Assistant professor on the Investigator Track, Division of Rheumatology",
      "description": "Department Department of Medicine Division IM - Rheumatology Track Tenure Rank Assistant Professor Title Assistant professor on the Investigator Track, Division of Rheumatology Position Description The Rheumatology Division in the Department of Medicine of the Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis is seeking a instructor in medicine. &nbsp; Washington University Rheumatology Division provides leading care for patients with rheumatic diseases (arthritis, musculoskeletal, autoimmune, and inflammatory conditions) and offers a level of experience and expertise available at few centers in the nation. We treat a wide range of common and complex rheumatic diseases including many types of arthritis and vasculitis, as well as other rare connective tissue diseases. Special Instructions Please send inquiries to and/or submit your letter of interest and CV for immediate consideration to: &nbsp; Glenda Bullock Washington University School of Medicine Director of Research and Business Administration 660 South Euclid, Campus Box 8125 St. Louis, MO&nbsp; 63110 gbullock@wustl.edu Contact Name Kelly Nessel Contact Email nesselk@wustl.edu Contact Phone 314-313-3631 Posting Date 10/1/2021 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
