    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010542": {
      "title": "Dermatopathologist-Dermatologist",
      "description": "Department Department of Medicine Division IM - Dermatology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Dermatopathologist-Dermatologist Position Description The Department of Medicine, Division of Dermatology, and the Department of Pathology at Washington University School of Medicine are seeking a full-time, board certified/eligible dermatopathologist-dermatologist for a joint position in Dermatology and Pathology. Our Dermatopathology Center is a dynamic and growing service, with a wide variety of inflammatory and neoplastic cases from outpatient and inpatient academic settings, as well as from practitioners in the community. &nbsp; Our physicians and laboratory staff integrate a full range of diagnostic tests in our state-of-the-art facility located in the heart of the academic medical center. &nbsp; Our Dermatology clinical practice is comprised of over 20 dermatologists, many with a sub-specialty interest, drawing cases from a large regional catchment area. &nbsp; We are part of the Washington University Physician network, with access to nationally-recognized specialists across medical fields. &nbsp; The proportion of time spent in each discipline is flexible, but current expectation is at least 0.5 FTE in dermatopathology with additional FTE in clinical dermatology. &nbsp; A particular interest in medical education, with emphasis on teaching residents and fellows in dermatopathology, is preferred. &nbsp; The position will be at a level commensurate with experience. &nbsp; Ranked among the top five medical schools in the country by U.S. News &amp; World Report , WUSM and BJH, which is perennially ranked as one of the top 10 hospitals, offer a highly collegial environment within which to work and learn. &nbsp; Candidates must have completed an accredited dermatology residency and dermatopathology fellowship. &nbsp; A highly competitive compensation and incentive package will be offered to the successful candidate. Basic Qualifications Board eligible in both Dermatology and Dermatopathology. Special Instructions Contact: &nbsp; Ilana Rosman, MD Director, Dermatopathology Washington University School of Medicine 314-362-5757 irosman@wustl.edu &nbsp; Lynn Cornelius, MD Division Chief, Dermatology Washington University School of Medicine 314-362-8187 cornelil@wustl.edu &nbsp; Joseph Gaut, MD, PhD Division Chief, Anatomic and Molecular Pathology Washington University School of Medicine 314-747-2541 jpgaut@wustl.edu Contact Name Ilana Rosman, MD Director, Dermatopathology Contact Email irosman@wustl.edu Contact Phone 314-362-5757 Posting Date 1/1/2021 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
    },
    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010333": {
      "title": "CARDIOLOGY: Faculty – General Cardiology",
      "description": "Department Department of Medicine Division IM - Cardiology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title CARDIOLOGY: Faculty – General Cardiology Position Description The Cardiovascular Division, Department of Medicine, Washington University School of Medicine is a national leader in the delivery of high-quality cardiovascular care to a large, diverse patient population with a range of cardiovascular care needs, in training the next generation of leaders in cardiovascular medicine, and in conducting basic, translational, clinical, and population research to improve cardiovascular outcomes. To expand its outpatient practice, the Division is seeking general and preventative cardiologists at all ranks (Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor).&nbsp;&nbsp; The Division has one of the largest programs for comprehensive cardiac care in the Midwest, encompassing the full range of cardiology and its subspecialties. The general cardiology group incorporates practices at the Center for Advanced Medicine, and its two outreach sites in West and South St. Louis County, and contributes to inpatient cardiology care in the CCU, high-risk cardiology service, and the cardiology consultation service. A leadership position as Lead Physician for the West County practice is available for an appropriately qualified individual. The West County practice is closely linked with the Heart Care Institute, which houses an outpatient cardiac catheterization laboratory, cardiac diagnostic laboratory (including echocardiography, nuclear studies and SPECT imaging, vascular imaging, and cardiopulmonary stress testing), and comprehensive cardiac rehabilitation facility. The practice is supported by an extensive network of collaborative services, including advanced cardiac imaging, cardiothoracic surgery, electrophysiology and arrhythmia management, interventional cardiology, cardio-oncology, adult congenital heart disease, high risk obstetrics/maternal cardiology, pulmonary hypertension, and advanced heart failure and cardiac transplantation. The general cardiovascular disease fellowship trains nine fellows a year, and also has several fellows undergoing training via the physician-scientist training pathway. The Division supports a large number of clinical research investigations and clinical trials. Basic Qualifications The candidate should be an MD or DO board-certified in adult cardiovascular disease&nbsp; and should be well-versed in ambulatory general cardiology. Interest in cardiac imaging, including 2-D transthoracic, transesophageal, 3D, and stress echocardiography is desirable. Inpatient cardiology time and diagnostic cardiac catheterization interest can be accommodated. &nbsp; Additional Qualifications &nbsp; Special Instructions Applicants should mail or e- mail to:&nbsp; Sumanth Prabhu, MD &nbsp; (prabhu @wustl.edu ) his/her curriculum vitae and a letter stating career goals to the: Division of Cardiology, 660 South Euclid Avenue,&nbsp; MSC 8086-43-13, St. Louis, MO 63110. Contact Name Dr. Sumanth Prabhu Contact Email prabhu@wustl.edu Contact Phone 3143628908 Posting Date 9/22/2020 End Date No end date Reopened Date 1/14/2020 EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
    },
    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010173": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/Associate Professor - Clinician Educator, Division of Allergy &amp; Immunology",
      "description": "Department Department of Medicine Division IM - Immunology Track Clinician Rank Assistant Professor Title Assistant Professor/Associate Professor - Clinician Educator, Division of Allergy &amp; Immunology Position Description Instructor/Assistant Professor/Associate Professor – Clinician Educator &nbsp; The Allergy &amp; Immunology &nbsp; Division of the Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis is seeking a BC/BE allergist/immunologist to be appointed at the level of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor. &nbsp; Washington University Allergy and Immunology specialists provide comprehensive evaluation and management of patients with allergies, asthma, chronic sinusitis, allergic rhinitis (hayfever), urticaria (hives) and drug sensitivity. The board-certified physicians in this group also have broad experience in the diagnosis and management of rarer and more difficult-to-treat inherited and acquired immunodeficiency disorders that lead to recurrent skin and respiratory tract infections. &nbsp; Our offices serve as a resource to physicians and patients for diagnosis and treatment of allergic and immunological disorders ranging from the ordinary to the most challenging. Basic Qualifications Requirements and Essential Functions Board Certified/Board Eligible Allergist/Immunologist Successful completion of Allergy &amp; Immunology Fellowship Individuals with specific interest in Allergy &amp; Immunology are strongly encouraged to apply Desire and ability to participate in teaching with protected time for clinical research and&nbsp; &nbsp; publications, if desired. Special Instructions Please submit your letter of interest and CV for immediate consideration to: &nbsp; Maya Jerath, MD, PhD Washington University School of Medicine Division of Allergy &amp; Immunology, Division Chief 660 South Euclid, Campus Box 8122 St. Louis, MO &nbsp; 63110 mjerath@wustl.edu Contact Name Dr. Maya Jerath Contact Email mjereth@wustl.edu Contact Phone 