    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010457": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Medicine - Pulmonary and Critical Care Medicine",
      "description": "Department Department of Medicine Division IM - Pulmonary Diseases Track Research Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Medicine - Pulmonary and Critical Care Medicine Position Description Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis Missouri Department of Medicine seeks full-time Investigator/Tenure Track Faculty Members (Assistant/Associate Professor) in Pulmonary and Critical Care Medicine. Any topical area of lung biology or disease or related area will be considered. Basic Qualifications The position requires an M.D. and/or PhD. Interested applicants should send a letter of inquiry, their curriculum vitae and description of prior experience and future plans, and three letters of reference to: Michael J. Holtzman, MD at mjholtzman@wustl.edu . &nbsp; Contact Name Michael Holtzman Contact Email mjholtzman@wustl.edu Contact Phone 3143628970 Posting Date 11/27/2019 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
