    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010356": {
      "title": "Palliative Care Physician Educator",
      "description": "Department Department of Medicine Division IM - Palliative Medicine Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Palliative Care Physician Educator Position Description Position responsibilities include: Attending on the hospital-based palliative consult service Developing curricula Teaching at all levels of medical education Basic Qualifications Candidates must have board certification or board eligibility in palliative medicine.&nbsp; Strong preference will be given to candidates who have completed fellowship in palliative care. Contact Name Patrick White MD, HMDC, FACP, FAAHPM Contact Email patrick.white@bjc.org Contact Phone 314-609-2470 Posting Date 1/17/2019 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, rel