    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010099": {
      "title": "Inpatient General Neurology Faculty",
      "description": "Department Department of Neurology Division Neurology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Inpatient General Neurology Faculty Position Description The Department of Neurology at Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis, Missouri is seeking a BC/BE Neurologist (US or any system recognized as compatible for patient care purposes in the US) with special interest in hospital-based neurology. This position primarily entails evaluating and treating a wide range of patients as part of an academic teaching general neurology service. &nbsp; Prior experience and/or sub-specialty training is welcomed. &nbsp; Outpatient neurology practice opportunities are also part of the position. &nbsp; Interest in health outcomes, quality-improvement or clinical/translational research is encouraged. &nbsp;&nbsp; The Department of Neurology employs over 140 faculty and offers neurological care in all subspecialties. Affiliated hospitals include Barnes-Jewish (BJH), St. Louis Children’s Hospital (SLCH), and the Rehabilitation Institute of St. Louis. &nbsp; Contact Name Arun Varadhachary, MD Contact Email varadhacharya@wustl.edu Contact Phone 314-747-0644 Posting Date 1/10/2017 End Date 12/31/2026 Reopened Date 2/24/2026 EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 19