    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010045": {
      "title": "Pediatric Anesthesiologist",
      "description": "Department Department of Anesthesiology Division Anesthesiology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Pediatric Anesthesiologist Position Description The Department of Anesthesiology at Washington University School of Medicine is seeking a full-time Pediatric Anesthesiologist to join the Division of Pediatric Anesthesiology.&nbsp;&nbsp;In this exciting opportunity, you will join a thriving and dedicated group of 34 Pediatric Anesthesiologists, 26 CRNAs, Pediatric Anesthesiology Fellows, 4 Nurse practitioners, and 5 Administrators with a unified focus on excellence in patient care and innovation.&nbsp;&nbsp;This group provides clinical care at the nationally ranked St. Louis Children’s Hospital, the Shriners Hospital for Children, and the Children’s Specialty Care Centers in West and South Counties, performing ~30,000 cases annually across facilities. Many faculty and staff hold leadership roles in the areas of clinical operations, education, and research throughout the Washington University and Barnes Jewish Hospital systems.&nbsp; The Division of Pediatric Anesthesiology critically supports a shared academic mission with the Department of Anesthesiology by providing clinical, educational, and research training to medical students, Anesthesiology residents, and Pediatric Anesthesiology fellows. This shared mission includes a commitment to the development of faculty at all stages of their careers. The ideal candidate is intellectually curious, clinically skilled, able to work congenially with peers, and motivated for life-long learning. Compensation and Benefits Competitive Compensation with full health benefits Faculty Development Opportunities Retention bonus up to $60,000 31 days of PTO and 6 holidays Immediate University 403b match up to $34,500 Substantial Tuition Benefit with 7 years of service About Us The Washington University in Saint Louis Department of Anesthesiology and Pain Medicine has over 200 faculty members and is a national and international leader in clinical care, innovation and research.&nbsp; The medical center is geographically located in a beautiful setting next to Forest Park, a 1300-acre facility that is one of the largest urban parks in the United States! St. Louis is a vibrant metropolitan area with multiple eclectic neighborhoods, a healthy arts environment, a foodie scene as well as nationally ranked professional baseball, soccer, and hockey teams. For more information, kindly visit the Pediatric Anesthesiology Division Website:&nbsp; https://anesthesiology.wustl.edu/patient-care/pediatric-anesthesiology/ &nbsp;,&nbsp; the St. Louis Children’s Hospital Website:&nbsp; &nbsp; https://www.stlouischildrens.org/ &nbsp; and the following websites for St. Louis fun activities:&nbsp;&nbsp; https://www.explorestlouis.com &nbsp;and&nbsp; https://thestl.com &nbsp; Basic Qualifications Board Certification in Anesthesiology Board Certification in Pediatric Anesthesiology is preferred. Applicants with a strong commitment to building a collaborative culture and the exploration of novel approaches to fellowship training are encouraged &nbsp; Applicants with a management style that emphasizes teamwork, communication, collegiality, flexibility, trust and patience are encouraged communication, collegiality, fle xibility, trust, and patience are encouraged Special Instructions Interested applicants should send a letter of interest and their curriculum vitae to Dr. Dolores Njoku.&nbsp; &nbsp; Contact Information: Dolores Njoku, MD The Wise Professor of Anesthesiology Division Chief, Pediatric Anesthesiology and Vice Chair Department of Anesthesiology Washington University School of Medicine Pediatric Anesthesiologist-in-Chief St. Louis Children’s Hospital njoku@wustl.edu Contact Name Dr. Dolores Njoku Contact Email njoku@wustl.edu Posting Date 3/19/2025 End Date No end date Reopened Date 11/24/2021 EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
