    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010235": {
      "title": "Critical Care Medicine",
      "description": "Department Department of Anesthesiology Division Anesthesiology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Critical Care Medicine Position Description The Washington University School of Medicine - Anesthesiology Department is seeking a qualified individual to join a multidisciplinary group of intensivists in the Anesthesiology Critical Care Medicine (ACCM) Division. &nbsp;The position will include a balance of clinical time in critical care practice supporting community hospital sites and ICU telemedicine. &nbsp;Interest in education, leadership and administration are encouraged and will be supported with non-clinical time, mentoring and opportunities for advanced training to match the interests of the applicant. Strengths of the program include integration of an ICU telemedicine program to support academic and community critical care practice, and to provide programmatic support for quality improvement projects as well as other novel explorations in critical care.&nbsp; Basic Qualifications Requirements include successful completion of an ACGME-approved fellowship in Critical Care Medicine. Board certification or eligibility in Anesthesiology, Emergency Medicine, Internal Medicine or Surgery. Board certification or eligibility in critical care medicine by the American Board of Anesthesiology, American Board of Internal Medicine, American Board of Emergency Medicine or American Board of Surgery. Additional Qualifications Missouri State Medical License Illinois State Medical License Contact Email anest-icujobs@email.wustl.edu Posting Date 12/12/2017 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, 