    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010093": {
      "title": "Regional Anesthesiologist",
      "description": "Department Department of Anesthesiology Division Anesthesiology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Regional Anesthesiologist Position Description The Department of Anesthesiology at Washington University School of Medicine is seeking a full time Regional Anesthesiologist faculty member in the Division of Regional and Ambulatory Anesthesiology.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Faculty appointment level will depend on the applicant’s credentials and experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The division is currently made up of 8 faculty members providing clinical service for the operating rooms at Barnes-Jewish Hospital in St Louis.&nbsp; The faculty member is also expected to be active in the academic missions of the department, teaching fellows and residents.&nbsp;&nbsp; The Department, which has a total of 140 faculty, is also a national leader in research and will provide a rich environment for applicants that are looking to develop their research based interests along with clinical teaching.&nbsp; &nbsp; Basic Qualifications Anesthesiology Board certified or eligible and Fellowship trained in Regional Anesthesiology Contact Name Mitchell Fingerman Contact Email mitchellfingerman@wustl.edu Posting Date 5/22/2017 End Date No end date Reopened Date 2/14/2017 EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 50