    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010593": {
      "title": "General Radiologist - Phelps Health",
      "description": "Department Department of Radiology Division Diagnostic Radiology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title General Radiologist - Phelps Health Position Description The Mallinckrodt Institute of Radiology (MIR) through Washington University Regional Physicians seeks a Board Eligible/Certified full-time general radiologist with some experience in light interventional procedures at Phelps Health in Rolla, Missouri for its expanding Section of Washington University Regional Physicians/Community Radiology group.&nbsp; This position will also have a courtesy faculty appointment with the Washington University School of Medicine. Rolla, with a population of about 20,000, is located in Phelps County, which less than 100 miles from St. Louis, Columbia, and Springfield, Missouri.&nbsp; Rolla is in close proximity to the Mark Twain National Forest, Maramec Spring Park and has been identified \"101 Best Outdoor\" towns with many springs, forests, and rivers.&nbsp; Phelps County has 3 designated blue ribbon trout streams.&nbsp; Check http://mdc.mo.gov/fishing/species/trout/trout-areas &nbsp;to learn about Missouri Trout fishing other outdoor activities! Although we are based in St. Louis City, our community radiology section provides a broad range of advanced imaging procedures to hospitals and outpatient clinics serving St. Charles, St. Louis, and Phelps Counties. Mallinckrodt Institute of Radiology (MIR) is comprised of a large multi-specialty collaborative faculty and is one of the preeminent academic radiology departments in the nation. We use disease-specific protocols, perform quality imaging exams and provide accurate and in-depth interpretations. Not all imaging centers and radiologists are alike. Our expertise and the time we take for tests often eliminates the need for more We use disease-specific protocols, perform quality imaging exams and provide accurate and in-depth interpretations. Not all imaging centers and radiologists are alike. Our expertise and the time we take for tests often eliminates the need for more imaging exams and reduces patients' exposure to radiation. We provide pediatric and adult radiologic services. Basic Qualifications Qualified applicants should have a diverse diagnostic skillset appropriate for our dynamic and growing practice. Desirable attributes include the ability to read emergency department cases, mammography, and general invasive procedures including CT/ultrasound biopsies, myelograms, etc. Fellowship training in abdominal imaging is highly recommended. General Radiologist experience ideally with basic interventional skills. Special Instructions Compensation and Benefits: - Salary up $600,000 annually, which includes a geographic differential. - 20 vacation days (increasing to 22 days after 3 years). - Additional paid professional development days. - Comprehensive healthcare coverage. - Generous 403b matching. - Incidence-based malpractice insurance. - College tuition benefit for dependents. We provide our radiologists with generous benefits that include health, life and disability coverage, retirement and tuition assistance.&nbsp; In addition to these competitive benefits, the university offers a variety of time off and quality-of-life programs.&nbsp;&nbsp;We are a diverse group and wholly encourage diversity to reflect the rich community in which we live and serve. We are committed to promoting an environment that is inclusive and welcoming to all individuals. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, veteran status, disability or genetic information. Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, CV, and contact information for three references. &nbsp;https://www.mir.wustl.edu/ Contact Email MIRRecruiting@email.wustl.edu Posting Date 5/1/2026 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
    },
    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010594": {
      "title": "General Radiologist-Missouri Baptist Medical Center",
      "description": "Department Department of Radiology Division Diagnostic Radiology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title General Radiologist-Missouri Baptist Medical Center Position Description Mallinckrodt Institute of Radiology (MIR) through Washington University Regional Physicians is seeking full-time general radiologists for positions at Missouri Baptist Medical Center (426 bed tertiary care center) in west county St. Louis. These positions will also have a courtesy faculty appointment with Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis and opportunities to regularly participate in educational activities and career development opportunities at MIR.&nbsp; A state of the art SECTRA PACS system and EPIC EMR support efficient workflows. MIR is staffed with globally-recognized radiologists with subspecialty training who provide a full range of diagnostic imaging procedures for both pediatric and adult patients.&nbsp; In addition, our equipment is among the most advanced available and includes state-of-the-art ultrasound, magnetic resonance imaging (MRI), dedicated PET/MRI, and dual energy CT scanners with advanced imaging and 3D processing workstations. Basic Qualifications Applicants are expected to be board certified or eligible in radiology and must have a diverse diagnostic skillset appropriate for a dynamic, growing practice. This includes an ability to read emergency department cases, mammography, and general invasive procedures including CT/ultrasound biopsies, myelograms, etc.&nbsp; Subspecialty training in breast, musculoskeletal, neuro and abdominal imaging is desirable.&nbsp; Fellowship training is preferred but not required if candidate has substantial relevant practice experience. Special Instructions We are committed to promoting an environment that is inclusive and welcoming to all individuals. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, gender, sexual orien