    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010556": {
      "title": "Missouri Baptist Radiologist-Sullivan, MO",
      "description": "Department Department of Radiology Division Diagnostic Radiology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Missouri Baptist Radiologist-Sullivan, MO Position Description Mallinckrodt Institute of Radiology (MIR) through Washington University Regional Physicians is seeking a full-time general radiologist at Missouri Baptist Hospital in Sullivan, Missouri. &nbsp;&nbsp; The position will also provide services at Missouri Baptist Hospital and have a courtesy faculty appointment with Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis. MIR is staffed with globally-recognized radiologists with subspecialty training who provide a full range of diagnostic imaging procedures for both pediatric and adult patients. In addition, our equipment is among the most advanced available and includes state-of-the-art ultrasound, magnetic resonance imaging (MRI), dedicated PET/MRI, and dual energy CT scanners with advanced imaging and 3D processing workstations. Basic Qualifications Applicants are expected to be board certified or eligible in radiology and must have a diverse diagnostic skillset appropriate for a dynamic, growing practice. This includes an ability to read emergency department cases, mammography with breast procedures (biopsies and localizations) , and general invasive procedures (Aspirations, Arthrograms and minor procedures) including CT/ultrasound biopsies, myelograms, etc. &nbsp; Fellowship training is preferred but not required if candidate has substantial relevant practice experience . Special Instructions We are committed to promoting an environment that is inclusive and welcoming to all individuals. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, veteran status, disability or genetic information. &nbsp; Benefits MIR provides radiologist with generous benefits that include health, life and di