    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010945": {
      "title": "Diagnostic Radiologist - Onsite - Phelps and Sullivan",
      "description": "Department Department of Radiology Division Diagnostic Radiology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Diagnostic Radiologist - Onsite - Phelps and Sullivan Position Description Work Location: Onsite, providing coverage for Phelps County Regional Medical Center and Missouri Baptist Sullivan We are currently seeking a Diagnostic Onsite Radiologist for an exciting and rewarding opportunity at the prestigious Mallinckrodt Institute of Radiology at Washington University. The chosen candidate will be providing coverage for Phelps County Regional Medical Center and Missouri Baptist Sullivan. &nbsp; These two rural hospitals are located in south central Missouri in close proximity to each other. Rolla, with a population of about 20,000, is located in Phelps County, which is less than 100 miles from St. Louis, Columbia, and Springfield, Missouri. &nbsp; Rolla is in close proximity to the Mark Twain National Forest, Maramec Spring Park and has been identified \"101 Best Outdoor\" towns with many springs, forests, and rivers. &nbsp; Sullivan is located at the intersection of Interstate 44 and Missouri Route 185. Meramec State Park is east of the city. &nbsp; The driving distance between Rolla and Sullivan is approximately 40 miles. - Monday to Friday, 7AM to 4PM. - Approximately 80% time in Rolla and 20% time in Sullivan. - No nights or call coverage - Ability to earn additional compensation for paid weekend and off hours coverage. Basic Qualifications - Provide expert onsite radiological interpretation of imaging studies and minor procedures. - Analyze and interpret radiographs, MRI, fluoroscopy, ultrasound, CT scans and &nbsp; mammography. - Collaborate with other medical staff to improve patient care. - Provide timely and high-quality reports and consultation on patient findings. - Participate in multidisciplinary conferences to recommend patient treatment plans. - Adhere to all departmental procedures and quality standards. Additional Qualifications - Board-certified or board-eligible in Diagnostic Radiology. - Proficiency in interpreting ultrasound and CT scans. - No MR interpretation required. Please note: This position is not visa eligible. Special Instructions Compensation and Benefits: - Salary up to $600,000 annually, which includes a geographic differential. - 20 vacation days (increasing to 22 days after 3 years). - Additional paid professional development days. - Comprehensive healthcare coverage. - Generous 403b matching. - Incidence-based malpractice insurance. - College tuition benefit for dependents. We are committed to offering competitive compensation and a comprehensive benefits package. If you are looking to work at a top-tier institute and have the necessary skills and experience, we would love to hear from you. Washington University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status. Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, CV, and contact information for three references. Contact Name Dr. Pamela Woodard Contact Email woodardp@wustl.edu Posting Date 5/1/2026 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
