    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1011141": {
      "title": "General and Subspecialty Radiologist - Community (Remote Overnight)",
      "description": "Department Department of Radiology Division Diagnostic Radiology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title General and Subspecialty Radiologist - Community (Remote Overnight) Position Description Mallinckrodt Institute of Radiology (MIR) at Washington University School of Medicine seeks a dedicated remote overnight radiologist to join our Community Division (TeleMIR). You will provide teleradiology coverage overnight (11PM–7AM CT) for BJC-affiliated hospitals across Illinois, including Memorial Hospital Belleville and Memorial Hospital Shiloh. The schedule is 1 week on / 2 weeks off, offering significant work-life balance. TeleMIR is MIR’s emergency teleradiology service providing overnight coverage for community hospitals. Key Responsibilities - Interpret emergency and inpatient studies (primarily CT, X-ray/US and occasional MRI) overnight. - Communicate findings promptly to ordering providers. - Uphold high quality standards in a fast-paced environment. Schedule &amp; Compensation - Schedule: 7 consecutive nights on, 14 nights off (approx. 17 weeks/year) - Hours: 11:00PM–7:00AM CT - Salary: $500,000–$550,000/year (commensurate with experience) - Supplemental income: Additional moonlighting opportunities available - Benefits: Washington University faculty benefits package (see: https://hr.wustl.edu/benefits/) - Malpractice: Incident-based malpractice coverage provided About Mallinckrodt Institute of Radiology (MIR) MIR is the academic radiology department of Washington University School of Medicine, performing ~2 million imaging procedures annually. It ranks among the top NIH-funded radiology departments and is a global leader in research, education, and radiologic innovation. About BJC HealthCare &amp; Illinois Hospital Partners BJC HealthCare is a non-profit system that operates hospitals in Missouri and Illinois, including Barnes-Jewish Hospital and St. Louis Children’s Hospital. MIR provides remote imaging services for Illinois-based hospitals Alton Memorial Hospital, &nbsp;Memorial Hospital Belleville and Memorial Hospital Shiloh, both known for high-quality community care. Why Join Us? - Flexible scheduling and fully remote work model - Strong institutional support and academic affiliation - Moonlighting opportunities to supplement income - Access to Washington University’s full benefits package - Incident-based malpractice coverage - Be part of a mission-driven, collaborative TeleMIR team &nbsp; &nbsp; Basic Qualifications - ABR board certified or eligible - Eligible for Illinois and Missouri licensure - Proficient in emergency CT and routine inpatient imaging - Excellent communication skills - Teleradiology experience preferred but not required Contact Name Andy Bierhals, MD, MPH, FACR Contact Email bierhals@wustl.edu Posting Date 5/1/2026 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
    },
    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1011221": {
      "title": "General and Subspecialty Radiologist – Community (Remote through TeleMIR)",
      "description": "Department Department of Radiology Division Community Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title General and Subspecialty Radiologist – Community (Remote through TeleMIR) Position Description Mallinckrodt Institute of Radiology (MIR) &nbsp;seeks dedicated full-time and part-time remote radiologists to join our Community Division (TeleMIR). You will provide teleradiology services for evening and deep night shifts for BJC-affiliated hospitals across Illinois. MIR is the radiology department for &nbsp;Washington University School of Medicine, with a growing Community Division.&nbsp;&nbsp; MIR performs ~2 million imaging procedures annually. It is a global leader in research, education, and radiologic innovation. Key Responsibilities - Interpret emergency and inpatient studies (primarily CT, X-ray/US and occasional MRI) overnight. - Communicate findings promptly to ordering providers. - Uphold high-quality standards in a fast-paced environment. Schedules &amp; Compensation Full-Time Radiologist : - Salary: $500,000–$550,000/year &nbsp; - $40,000 Signing Bonus for candidates committing to an evening or deep night schedule &nbsp; - Choice of Schedule:&nbsp; - Evening 5:00 pm-1:00 AM CT; 1 week on and 1 week off - Deep Nights 11:00 PM-7:00 AM CT; 1 week on 2 weeks off - Generous Benefit Package: - Dependent Tuition Assistance – up to 100% tuition and fees paid - Parent/Caregiver Leave – 12 weeks paid leave; additional 12 weeks at 60% pay if eligible &nbsp; &nbsp; Per Diem and/or Moonlighting opportunities available: - Per Diem Evenings 5PM-1AM - $4000/shift - Per Diem Deep Nights 11PM-7AM - $4500/shift - Per Diem Weekend. Daytime 8 hrs - $3500/shift - Malpractice: Incident-based malpractice coverage provided &nbsp; Basic Qualifications Basic Qualifications - ABR board certified or eligible - Eligible for Illinois and Missouri licensure - Proficient in emergency CT and routine inpatient imaging - Excellent communication skills - Teleradiology experience preferred but not required Special Instructions About BJC HealthCare &amp; Illinois Hospital Partners BJC HealthCare is a non-profit system that operates hospitals in Missouri and Illinois, including Barnes-Jewish Hospital and St. Louis Children’s Hospital. MIR provides remote imaging services for Illinois-based hospitals, Alton Memorial Hospital, Memorial Hospital Belleville, and Memorial Hospital Shiloh, all of which are known for high-quality community care. Why Join Us? - Fully remote work model - Flexible scheduling - Strong institutional support and academic affiliation - Moonlighting opportunities to supplement income - Access to Washington University’s full benefits package - Incident-based malpractice coverage - Be part of a mission-driven, collaborative TeleMIR team Posting Date 5/1/2026 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
