    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010513": {
      "title": "Interventional Radiologist",
      "description": "Department Department of Radiology Division Diagnostic Radiology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Interventional Radiologist Position Description T he Mallinckrodt Institute of Radiology at the Washington University School of Medicine, St Louis, MO is seeking an Interventional Radiologist to join our academic group, which includes 17 faculty attendings, one medical physicist, 9 physician assistants, 10 nurse coordinators and 2 medical/administrative assistants.&nbsp; Our department also has ACGME approved independent and integrated IR training pathways. Established in 1987, our interventional radiology section is one of the largest and most comprehensive IR groups in the nation. More than 60,000 IR procedures are performed each year encompassing adult, pediatric, vascular and non-vascular procedures.&nbsp; The practice location will be substantially located at our academic campus, which includes new patient-facing IR clinics in close proximity to the procedural areas.&nbsp; Our facilities are state of the art and will soon be expanded by the addition of a new patient tower that will house a new central IR workplace with 4 angio suites, a hybrid CT-angio suite and 2 procedural CTs.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; Basic Qualifications Applicants should be ABR certified or ABR eligible with either an M.D. or M.D., Ph.D. and fellowship training in interventional radiology. Applicants should be experienced in the broad spectrum of IR procedures and be interested in playing a key role in training an immensely talented group of more than 70 Radiology residents.&nbsp; We have opportunities for clinical development, teaching, research and national involvement.&nbsp; Members of the section are quite active in many national organizations. Additional Qualifications &nbsp; Special Instructions Compensation and Benefits: - Competitive Salary package - 22 vacation days annually - Comprehensive healthcare coverage. - Generous 403b matching. - Incidence-based malpractice insurance. - College tuition benefit for dependents. We provide our radiologists with generous benefits that include health, life and disability coverage, retirement and tuition assistance.&nbsp; In addition to these competitive benefits, the university offers a variety of time off and quality-of-life programs.&nbsp;&nbsp;We are a diverse group and wholly encourage diversity to reflect the rich community in which we live and serve. We are committed to promoting an environment that is inclusive and welcoming to all individuals. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, veteran status, disability or genetic information. Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, CV, and contact information for three references. &nbsp; https://www.mir.wustl.edu/ &nbsp; Contact Email MIRRecruiting@email.wustl.edu Posting Date 1/1/2026 End Date No end date Reopened Date 1/9/2025 EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in 