    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1011184": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Division of General Surgery, Section of Transplant Surgery",
      "description": "Department Department of Surgery Division General Surgery – Transplant Track Clinician Rank Assistant Professor Title Assistant Professor - Division of General Surgery, Section of Transplant Surgery Position Description The Division of General Surgery, Section of Transplant Surgery at Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis invites applications for a full-time faculty position within the division. The surgeon will be primarily based at Barnes Jewish Medical Center. Teaching duties will include teaching residents and oversee the clinical training of doctors.&nbsp; Will guide the resident doctors in a day to day patient care and explain proper patient care techniques and procedures. &nbsp; Basic Qualifications The successful candidate will need to be board certified and have completed a general surgery residency program and abdominal transplant surgery fellowship with proven leadership skills.&nbsp; Additional Qualifications Involvement with resident and medical student education and the pursuit of scholarly activities is expected. Applicants will need to demonstrate practical interpersonal and communication skills and be committed to ongoing performance improvement. Dedication to enhancing a diverse workforce and academic environment is vital.&nbsp; Posting Date 1/30/2026 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
