      "title": "Pediatric Otolaryngologist",
      "description": "Department Department of Otolaryngology Division Otolaryngology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Pediatric Otolaryngologist Position Description The Department of Otolaryngology – Head and Neck Surgery at Washington University seeks&nbsp;a&nbsp;fellowship-trained Pediatric Otolaryngologist.&nbsp; We seek individuals who are&nbsp;committed to an&nbsp;academic career in pediatric otolaryngology and&nbsp;to building a&nbsp;busy clinical practice.&nbsp; Research opportunities are available for candidates with&nbsp;training and an interest in pursuing&nbsp;independent investigator- initiated research.&nbsp; Basic Qualifications Applicants must be board certified or board&nbsp;eligible by the American Board of Otolaryngology &amp; have completed a pediatric otolaryngology fellowship. Appointment is contingent on successful acquisition of licensure in the state of Missouri and credentialing at St. Louis Children's Hospital.&nbsp; Posting Date 7/19/2023 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committe