    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1011046": {
      "title": "Faculty (Full Time): WUSM Division of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation (Interventional Spine)",
      "description": "Department Department of Orthopedic Surgery Division Orthopaedic Surgery Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Faculty (Full Time): WUSM Division of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation (Interventional Spine) Position Description The PM&amp;R Division of Washington University’s Department of Orthopaedic Surgery is seeking a&nbsp;full-time musculoskeletal clinical faculty member specializing in interventional spine to join our&nbsp;high-volume practice in St. Louis, MO. This role maximizes the benefits of an academic medical&nbsp;center, including: •&nbsp; &nbsp;Developing a full-time musculoskeletal physical medicine &amp; rehabilitation academic clinical&nbsp;practice focused on spine. •&nbsp; &nbsp;Providing interventional spine procedures for a busy multidisciplinary practice. •&nbsp; &nbsp;Active participation in physical medicine and rehabilitation resident and fellow education,&nbsp;conferences and journal clubs. •&nbsp; &nbsp;Conducting clinical, basic-science, translational and/or biomechanics research.&nbsp; Our vision is to grow our impact on musculoskeletal and spine care by improving access and&nbsp;outcomes, training the next generation of physiatric leaders, and transforming the future of care through discovery and innovation. Join us! Basic Qualifications All applicants must have completed PM&amp;R fellowship training in interventional spine procedures, or&nbsp;be in the process of completing fellowship.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Must be board eligible and&nbsp;be eligible to obtain a permanent MO medical license. Special Instructions Please email a letter of interest and curriculum vitae to Division Chief&nbsp;Devyani Hunt, MD, MS, at huntdm@wustl.edu Contact Email huntdm@wustl.edu Posting Date 7/9/2024 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
