      "title": "Faculty (Full-Time) - Foot-Ankle Division WUSM, Orthopedic Surgery",
      "description": "Department Department of Orthopedic Surgery Division Orthopaedic Surgery Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Faculty (Full-Time) - Foot-Ankle Division WUSM, Orthopedic Surgery Position Description Washington University School of Medicine’s Department of Orthopaedic Surgery — Foot and Ankle&nbsp;Division — seeks a full-time clinical faculty member, to join our high-volume practice. RESPONSIBILITIES Clinical:&nbsp; Clinical responsibilities of this position include developing a full-time foot and ankle&nbsp;academic clinical practice. •&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Washington University School of Medicine enjoys strong brand awareness and has a reputation&nbsp;for providing premier clinical care regionally and nationally. •&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; The foot and ankle division at Washington University Orthopedics has a regional and national&nbsp;reputation for excellence in care, from sports-related foot and ankle injuries to deformity&nbsp;correction. •&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Our specialists work as a multidisciplinary team to evaluate, diagnose and treat a wide&nbsp;array of foot and ankle conditions — from everyday sprains to the most complex non-healing&nbsp;fractures and arthritis. Academic Instruction: Academic responsibilities include active participation in, and commitment to,&nbsp;orthopedic&nbsp;fellow and resident education, including: •&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Clinical training and teaching. •&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Participating in conferences, journal clubs and related activities. Research: The faculty member will conduct research (clinical, basic science, translational and/or&nbsp;biomechanics), working with researchers within the department and&nbsp; &nbsp;cross Washington University&nbsp;School of Medicine. Our research coordinators have a long history of research contribution. Basic Qualifications All applicants must have completed, or be in the process of completing, a foot and ankle&nbsp;fellowship training program. All applicants must be board certified or board eligible, and must be&nbsp;eligible to obtain a permanent Missouri&nbsp;medical license. Additional Qualifications A dedication to excellence in patient care and teaching, and an interest in clinical, basic&nbsp;science, translational and/or biomechanics research. Special Instructions Please email a letter of interest and curriculum vitae to: Jeremy McCormick, MD Associate Professor, Orthopedic Surgery Chief, Foot and Ankle Division Director, Foot and Ankle Fellowship Program mccormickj@wustl.edu Contact Name Jeremy McCormick Contact Email mccormickj@wustl.edu Contact Phone 314-514-3569 Posting Date 6/18/2024 End Date No end date Reopened Date 6/18/2024 EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, 