    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010388": {
      "title": "Hem/Onc-Faculty Appointment (Investigator Track) #1010388",
      "description": "Department Department of Pediatrics Division Pediatrics-Hematology/Oncology Track Tenure Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Hem/Onc-Faculty Appointment (Investigator Track) #1010388 Position Description The Division of Hematology Oncology in the Department of Pediatric is seeking a board certified or board eligible pediatrician who has completed a three-year fellowship in pediatric hematology oncology to join our faculty on the Investigator Track, with a focus on benign hematology and related hematologic disorders such as disorders of hematopoietic components and/or the coagulation cascade. The position predominantly involves research time; clinical activities are restricted as described above. Basic Qualifications &nbsp; Ph.D. or M.D., Ph.D. Additional Qualifications &nbsp;Instructor or higher. Special Instructions Please contact Dr. Jorge Di Paola with any questions related to this posting. Contact Name Katrina Crawford Contact Email crawfordk@wustl.edu Posting Date 6/16/2026 End Date No end date Reopened Date 6/17/2026 EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
