      "title": "Assistant Professor (Clinician Track) - #1011215",
      "description": "Department Department of Pediatrics Division Pediatrics-Gastroenterology Track Clinician Rank Assistant Professor Title Assistant Professor (Clinician Track) - #1011215 Position Description We seek a board certified or board eligible pediatrician who has completed a three year fellowship in pediatric gastroenterology and a one year fellowship in pediatric transplant hepatology to join our faculty on the clinician track. The position predominantly involves patient care in ambulatory and inpatient settings, procedures, and teaching. Special interests within the field of pediatric hepatology are encouraged. Basic Qualifications MD Special Instructions Please contact Dr. Tarr with any questions related to this posting. Contact Name Phillip Tarr Contact Email tarr@wustl.edu Contact Phone 314-286-2848 Posting Date 4/21/2026 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in