    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1011208": {
      "title": "Pediatric Endocrinologist WURP Staff Physician (Springfield, Missouri) #1011208",
      "description": "Department Department of Pediatrics Division Peds Endocrinology &amp; Diabetes Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Pediatric Endocrinologist WURP Staff Physician (Springfield, Missouri) #1011208 Position Description St. Louis Children’s Hospital at Cox Healthcare in Springfield, Missouri and Washington University School of Medicine are seeking board certified/board eligible applicants for WashU Regional Physicians roles at the Springfield, Missouri location. The successful pediatric endocrinologist trained physician will join our existing team at the brand new Children’s Specialty Care Center (CSCC) location in Springfield, Missouri, slated to open in July of 2027. This dynamic team currently includes one Pediatric Endocrinologist as well as Peds GI, Peds Neurology, and Peds Sleep physicians. Outreach clinic support is also provided through St. Louis Children’s Hospital with Peds Urology, Peds Ophthalmology, Peds General Surgery, and Peds Hematology/Oncology. This position is primarily outpatient based with hospital consults at nearby Cox Medical Center South. Cox South has an exceptional 26-bed pediatric inpatient unit with Pediatric Hospitalist coverage, a 6-bed PICU covered by Pediatric Intensivists, and a 36-bed NICU with 24/7 coverage by Neonatologists and NNPs. Benefits include: · Highly competitive salary · Comprehensive benefits package, including a WashU tuition benefit · CME allowance &nbsp; Why Springfield Located in the scenic Ozarks, Springfield offers the perfect blend of big-city amenities and small-town charm. With a low cost of living, excellent schools, and easy access to outdoor recreation, Springfield is an ideal place to live and raise a family. Enjoy a vibrant arts scene, local dining, and a welcoming community that makes you feel right at home. Basic Qualifications Board certified/eligible in Pediatric Endocrinology Special Instructions Please visit our faculty jobs site at https://facultyopportunities.wu