    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1011209": {
      "title": "Pediatric Pulmonologist WURP Staff Physician (Springfield, Missouri) #",
      "description": "Department Department of Pediatrics Division Peds Allergy Immun Pulm Med Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Pediatric Pulmonologist WURP Staff Physician (Springfield, Missouri) # Position Description St. Louis Children’s Hospital at Cox Healthcare in Springfield, Missouri and Washington University School of Medicine are seeking board certified/board eligible applicants for WashU Regional Physicians roles at the Springfield, Missouri location. The successful pediatric pulmonology trained physician will join our existing team at the brand new Children’s Specialty Care Center (CSCC) location in Springfield, Missouri, slated to open in July of 2027. This dynamic team currently includes one Pediatric Endocrinologist as well as Peds GI, Peds Neurology, and Peds Sleep physicians. Outreach clinic support is also provided through St. Louis Children’s Hospital with Peds Urology, Peds Ophthalmology, Peds General Surgery, and Peds Hematology/Oncology. This position is primarily outpatient based with hospital consults at nearby Cox Medical Center South. Cox South has an exceptional 26-bed pediatric inpatient unit with Pediatric Hospitalist coverage, a 6-bed PICU covered by Pediatric Intensivists, and a 36-bed NICU with 24/7 coverage by Neonatologists and NNPs. Benefits include: · Highly competitive salary · Comprehensive benefits package, including a WashU tuition benefit · CME allowance &nbsp; Why Springfield Located in the scenic Ozarks, Springfield offers the perfect blend of big-city amenities and small-town charm. With a low cost of living, excellent schools, and easy access to outdoor recreation, Springfield is an ideal place to live and raise a family. Enjoy a vibrant arts scene, local dining, and a welcoming community that makes you feel right at home. Basic Qualifications Board certified/eligible in Pediatric Pulmonology Special Instructions Please visit our faculty jobs site at https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/ &nbsp;to submit your application under posting # For more information, you may: Contact Pediatrician in Chief, Matt Alder at alderm@wustl.edu Contact Name Katherine Krajcovic Contact Email kkrajcovic@wustl.edu Contact Phone 314-273-4430 Posting Date 4/13/2026 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
