    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1011203": {
      "title": "Pediatric Critical Care Medicine WURP Staff Physician (Springfield, Missouri) #1011203",
      "description": "Department Department of Pediatrics Division Pediatrics-Div of Critical Care Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Pediatric Critical Care Medicine WURP Staff Physician (Springfield, Missouri) #1011203 Position Description St. Louis Children’s Hospital at Cox Healthcare in Springfield, Missouri and Washington University School of Medicine are seeking applicants for WashU Regional Physicians roles at the Springfield, Missouri location. The successful critical care trained physician will join our existing team in providing coverage to our six-bed PICU at St. Louis Children’s Hospital at Cox Medical Center South. This long-established program serves more than 30 counties throughout Southwest Missouri and Northwest Arkansas. Cox South is a 706-bed facility which includes a six-bed PICU staffed by 2 full-time physicians with PRN assistance. The 33-bed Level III NICU is covered 24/7 by our team of Neonatologists and NNPs, and our 26-bed Pediatric Inpatient Unit is staffed by board-certified pediatric hospitalists. Other pediatric specialists include endocrinology, gastroenterology, neurology, and more. The Cox Air Care program and the Children's Ambulance provide services for newborn emergency transports. Cox South has been affiliated with the Children's Miracle Network since 1986. Benefits include: · Highly competitive salary · Comprehensive benefits package, including a WashU tuition benefit · CME allowance &nbsp; Why Springfield Located in the scenic Ozarks, Springfield offers the perfect blend of big-city amenities and small-town charm. With a low cost of living, excellent schools, and easy access to outdoor recreation, Springfield is an ideal place to live and raise a family. Enjoy a vibrant arts scene, local dining, and a welcoming community that makes you feel right at home. Basic Qualifications Board certified/eligible in Pediatric Critical Care Medicine Special Instructions Please visit our faculty jobs site at https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/ to submit your application under posting # 1011203 For more information, you may: Contact Matt Alder at alderm@wustl.edu Contact Name Katherine Krajcovic Contact Email kkrajcovic@wustl.edu Contact Phone 314-273-4430 Posting Date 4/8/2026 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustmen