    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1011186": {
      "title": "#1011186 Children’s Discovery Institute Scholar in Pediatric Pulmonary Diseases and Asthma",
      "description": "Department Department of Pediatrics Division Peds Allergy Immun Pulm Med Track Tenure Rank Assistant Professor Title #1011186 Children’s Discovery Institute Scholar in Pediatric Pulmonary Diseases and Asthma Position Description The Children’s Discovery Institute and Department of Pediatrics, Division of Allergy and Pulmonary Medicine seeks a Scholar at the Assistant Professor level to lead basic investigations into the host immune response to genetic therapies for pediatric pulmonary diseases, including Cystic Fibrosis Basic Qualifications Doctorate (PhD, MD or equivalent) and post doctoral research experience in cell biology, immunology, vectorology or related field. Additional Qualifications Expertise in evaluating T cell responses to viral gene therapy vectors is desired Special Instructions Please contact Dr. Rubenstein with any questions related to this posting. Contact Name Ron Rubenstein, M.D., Ph.D. Contact Email rubenstein@wustl.edu Contact Phone 314-286-2146 Posting Date 2/3/2026 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
