    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1011071": {
      "title": "PEM- Faculty member in the Division of Pediatric Emergency Medicine, Attending Physician Northwest Healthcare ED - #1011071",
      "description": "Department Department of Pediatrics Division Pediatric Emergency Medicine Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title PEM- Faculty member in the Division of Pediatric Emergency Medicine, Attending Physician Northwest Healthcare ED - #1011071 Position Description The Division of Pediatric Emergency Medicine at Washington University School of Medicine is seeking applicants for General Pediatricians (board certified/eligible) Or Pediatric Emergency Medicine physicians (board certified/eligible) for work in the Emergency Department at Northwest Healthcare, a suburban community hospital. &nbsp; Our general pediatricians join a collaborative division of Pediatric Emergency Medicine physicians. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Northwest Healthcare is a 24/7 stand-alone emergency department in north St. Louis County. &nbsp; The emergency department sees 11,000 pediatric patients each year. &nbsp; The Department of Pediatrics provides a supportive and intellectually stimulating environment for clinical practice, education and investigation, with unique opportunities for inter- and intra-departmental collaborations. &nbsp; The division supports faculty professional growth and leadership. &nbsp; Salary and benefits are competitive. Basic Qualifications Board Certified/Board Eligible Special Instructions Please contact Dr. Kimberly Quayle with any questions related to this posting. Contact Name Kimberly Quayle Contact Email quayleks@wustl.edu Contact Phone 314-454-2341 Posting Date 8/29/2024 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
