    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1011008": {
      "title": "#1011008 Clinical Pediatric Hematologist",
      "description": "Department Department of Pediatrics Division Pediatrics-Hematology/Oncology Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title #1011008 Clinical Pediatric Hematologist Position Description We seek a board certified or board eligible pediatrician who have completed a three-year fellowship in pediatric hematology oncology by time of appointment to join our faculty on the Clinician Track in the Hematology program. The position involves full-time direct patient care, including ambulatory care, inpatient responsibilities, and hematology consult service. Special interest/development in Sickle Cell Disease is preferred. Basic Qualifications Board Certified/Board Eligible &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; MD or MD, PHd Contact Name Katrina Crawford Contact Email crawfordk@wustl.edu Posting Date 4/17/2024 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
