    "https://facultyopportunities.wustl.edu/Posting/Detail/1010148": {
      "title": "Adult Primary Care Physician",
      "description": "Department Primary Care Division Washington University Clinical Associates (WUCA) Track Clinician Rank Commensurate w/Experience Title Adult Primary Care Physician Position Description At Washington University School of Medicine, we take pride in our mission to lead in the advancement of human health through the very best clinical care, innovative research and the education of tomorrow’s leaders in biomedicine, in a culture that supports diversity, inclusion, critical thinking and creativity. Primary care serves as a cornerstone of comprehensive health care for all patients and Washington University School of Medicine is expanding its primary care provider base as part of its mission. Washington University Clinical Associates (WUCA) is seeking general internal medicine physicians to join established primary care group practices located in the St. Louis, MO metropolitan area. WUCA physicians are provided a unique opportunity where they are employed by Washington University, with a voluntary faculty appointment at the School of Medicine, yet they practice in smaller group practices throughout the community.&nbsp; Our primary care physicians have an active, meaningful role in management of their clinical practices, in private practice-like settings, while enjoying the benefits and resources that come with being part of an academic organization.&nbsp;&nbsp; WUCA physicians are also often involved in teaching and mentoring medical students and residents. WUCA employed physicians have access to the University’s comprehensive benefit package.&nbsp; Eligible candidates may also have access to our Student Loan Assistance Program for educational loan forgiveness.&nbsp; Salaries are market competitive and commensurate with experience, with significant bonus opportunities available. Our openings are wonderful opportunities for new graduates or experienced MDs. For further information, please call or e-mail Sam O'Rourke 314-273-4879 or orourkes@wustl.edu. Basic Qualifications Medical Degree Special Instructions Interested candidates should submit their CV to: https://FacultyOpportunities.wustl.edu/apply and for further inquiries you may contact: Sam O'Rourke Director of Clinical Operations orourkes@wustl.edu 314-273-4879 Contact Name Sam O'Rourke Contact Email orourkes@wustl.edu Contact Phone (314) 273-6519 Posting Date 6/9/2017 End Date No end date EEO Statement Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. Apply Back to List 660 S. Euclid Ave. St. Louis, MO 63110-1010 Equal Employment Opportunity Washington University in St. Louis is committed to the principles and practices of equal employment opportunity. It is the University’s policy to provide equal opportunity and access to persons in all job titles without regard to race, ethnicity or shared ancestry, color, national origin, citizenship (where prohibited by federal law), age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. &nbsp; As a federal contractor, the university maintains affirmative action programs to implement its equal employment opportunity policy for individuals with disabilities and protected veterans, in accordance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 (VEVRAA), as amended. © 2026 Washington University in St. Louis Emergency Policies News "
    }
